      "section_title": "Q.1 Choose the correct answer of the following (any seven question\n                    only):",
      "total_marks": 2,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q1_1",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>What is the first step in the instruction execution cycle?</p>",
          "options": [
            "Decode",
            "Execute",
            "Fetch",
            "Store"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_2",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>What is the advantage of carry look-ahead adders over ripple carry adders?</p>",
          "options": [
            "Simplicity in design",
            "Increased latency",
            "Reduced power consumption",
            "Faster addition by reducing carry propagation delay"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_3",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>Which type of control unit is faster but more difficult to modify?</p>",
          "options": [
            "Hardwired Control Unit",
            "Microprogrammed Control Unit",
            "Cache Control Unit",
            "Memory Management Unit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_4",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following I/O transfer methods involves the CPU polling the device until data is\n                        ready?\n                    </p>",
          "options": [
            "DMA",
            "Interrupt-driven I/O",
            "Program-controlled I/O",
            "Asynchronous I/O"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_5",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>What does a branch prediction mechanism in a CPU help reduce?</p>",
          "options": [
            "Data hazards",
            "Structural hazards",
            "Control hazards",
            "Clock cycle delays"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_6",
          "type": "mcq",
